    25	| E | `cloudspring-bathhouse`, `button-and-spool`, `clockwork-observatory`, `coral-commons`, `meadow-post` | Calm, miniatures, celestial craft, underwater life and pastel comfort |
    26	
    27	## 1. The Monster Mailroom
    28	
    29	- **Genre:** friendly monster workplace ensembles; a busy dispatch floor run by gentle creatures. Wave A. ID `creature-dispatch`.
    30	- **Emotional target:** a bustling, warmhearted creature workplace; capable workers with comic physical variety.
    31	- **Composition/materials:** stepped parcel depot, frosted capsule tubes, ceramic counters, ribbed metal, soft overhead pools of light. Emphasize parcel routing; avoid any apparatus or set piece recognizable from an existing work.
    32	- **Art swatches:** seafoam `#78C5AF`, plum `#60476E`, butter `#F4D79A`, ink `#20323D`. Functional text contrast is checked separately.
    33	- **Cast order:** broad moss-furred courier; tall velvet moth clerk; squat stone sorter; long-necked feather archivist; round many-footed mechanic; small fin-eared inspector. Original faces and proportions; no likeness of any existing character, costume or insignia.
    34	- **Stations:** dispatch desk / fabrication dock / parcel archive / inspection counter / supervisor window / waiting platform (order: general/site/archive/verify/office/bench).
    35	- **Props:** parcel capsule, routing card, desk stamp, trolley, magnifier, tool pouch.
    36	- **Submission signature:** `capsule`, illustrated as a parcel entering a local receiving tray. Waiting workers hold a routing card; failed/lost states become still, attentive poses with the shared clear label.
    37	- **Candidate public description:** “An extraordinary crew keeps your work moving through a lively dispatch depot.”
    38	
    39	## 2. Little Helpers Laboratory
    40	
    41	- **Genre:** small-helper ensemble comedy; retro scientific workshops. Wave A. ID `pocket-lab`.
    42	- **Emotional target:** mischievous invention with readable, purposeful activity.
    43	- **Composition/materials:** cutaway laboratory, curved enamel worktops, chunky switches, instrument racks, borosilicate vessels. Amber task lights provide warmth without making workers a yellow-uniform swarm.
    44	- **Art swatches:** cobalt `#355C9B`, warm white `#EEE8DA`, coral `#E37E6A`, graphite `#253440`.
    45	- **Cast order:** cube-bodied display assistant; three-legged copper instrument; accordion-neck robot; ceramic sphere on tracks; articulated clamp helper; tiny multi-drawer automaton. Avoid any silhouette, colour and costume combination that recalls an existing mascot, and any copied voice.
    46	- **Stations:** experiment desk / prototype bench / specimen cabinet / calibration bay / lead scientist desk / charging nook.
    47	- **Props:** blueprint, coil, caliper, sample tray, work lamp, small trolley.
    48	- **Submission signature:** `spark`, a brief contained instrument glow rather than an explosion or evidence-of-success claim.
    49	- **Candidate description:** “Small inventors, oversized equipment, and a laboratory full of personality.”
    50	
    51	## 3. Heist Night
    52	
    53	- **Genre:** ensemble heist cinema; a calm, competent crew planning at night. Wave B. ID `midnight-bureau`.
    54	- **Emotional target:** calm competence, specialization and sophisticated teamwork.
    55	- **Composition/materials:** city-night planning office, walnut, brass, frosted glass, blue-lit drafting tables. Functional layers stay brighter than the moody background.
    56	- **Art swatches:** midnight `#172A3A`, champagne `#CDB78F`, walnut `#735743`, paper `#F0E8DB`.
    57	- **Cast order:** planner with rolled drawings; communications specialist with headset; researcher with tabbed notebook; logistics specialist with case; analyst with tablet; inspector with loupe. Original faces/clothes; no actor likenesses, film dialogue, real venue logos or copied promotional layouts.
    58	- **Stations:** briefing table / operations desk / dossier vault / audit table / director desk / lounge.
    59	- **Props:** dossier, blueprint roll, task lamp, case, route card, tabletop projector.
    60	- **Submission signature:** `dossier`, a crisp folder placement. Working motions are small hand/tool movements rather than physical comedy.
    61	- **Candidate description:** “A specialist crew turns a careful plan into coordinated work.”
    62	
    63	## 4. The Chocolate Factory
    64	
    65	- **Genre:** magical confectionery and theatrical invention; a candy factory as a stage. Wave C. ID `confectionery-works`.
    66	- **Emotional target:** wonder, craft and extravagant machinery.
    67	- **Composition/materials:** copper kettles, sugar-glass windows, plum tile and ribbon conveyors. Use an original floor plan and machinery; no recreation of a film set.
    68	- **Art swatches:** plum `#643B65`, copper `#B96F47`, raspberry `#D9618B`, cream `#F7E8CD`.
    69	- **Cast order:** flour-dusted pastry artisan; sugar-glass automaton; moth-winged wrapper; ceramic kettle attendant; ribbon-haired mixer; pear-shaped clockwork taster. Avoid any existing factory-worker or chocolatier character design, costume or lyrics.
    70	- **Stations:** recipe desk / invention kitchen / wrapped-goods shelves / inspection table / head confectioner desk / cooling rack.
    71	- **Props:** recipe card, mixing paddle, wrapped parcel, copper scoop, tasting tray, ribbon spool.
    72	- **Submission signature:** `parcel`, an original ribbon wrapping around an artifact token.
    73	- **Candidate description:** “An extravagant confectionery where every invention gets careful attention.”
    74	
    75	## 5. The Lantern Woods Guild
    76	
    77	- **Genre:** woodland fantasy adventure and craft guilds. Wave C. ID `lanternwood-guild`.
    78	- **Emotional target:** purposeful exploration, handmade tools and quiet magic.
    79	- **Composition/materials:** guild workshops inside a great tree, carved timber, mossy stone, blue-green glass and warm lanterns.
    80	- **Art swatches:** pine `#365D4D`, moss `#A2B67C`, lantern `#E8BC70`, slate `#314653`.
    81	- **Cast order:** mapmaker; horned woodland smith; bird courier; stone-bodied archivist; herbal engineer; cloak-wearing appraiser. Original outfits, species and symbols; no likeness of existing game heroes, emblems, recognizable gear or game interface.
    82	- **Stations:** quest desk / crafting bench / scroll archive / appraisal table / guild steward / travelers' rest.
    83	- **Props:** original map, lantern, scroll tube, hand tool, specimen basket, seal block.
    84	- **Submission signature:** `lantern`, a restrained glow above a submitted scroll, never an approval seal.
    85	- **Candidate description:** “A woodland guild of explorers and makers brings each assignment to life.”
    86	
    87	## 6. The Coffee House Crew
    88	
    89	- **Genre:** cozy ensemble sitcoms and neighborhood cafés. Wave C. ID `corner-cafe`.
    90	- **Emotional target:** companionship, approachable teamwork and familiar daily rituals.
    91	- **Composition/materials:** café/apartment-adjacent studio, amber lamps, brick, sage upholstery and sunlit windows. Original architecture and furniture, not a replica of any existing television set.
    92	- **Art swatches:** brick `#A75F4E`, sage `#93A58E`, amber `#D9AD65`, oat `#F0E7D8`.
    93	- **Cast order:** illustrator; bookish researcher; practical organizer; café host; architect; editor. Original adult ensemble, no actor likenesses, copied wardrobe, character names, dialogue or logo treatment.
    94	- **Stations:** window desk / shared worktable / bookshelf / reading table / host's desk / lounge nook.
    95	- **Props:** notebook, coffee cup, folder, drawing roll, desk lamp, book cart.
    96	- **Submission signature:** `dossier`, an understated folder handoff; no laugh track.
    97	- **Candidate description:** “A welcoming neighborhood workspace where everyone has a part to play.”
    98	
    99	## 7. Tumbletown Rhyme Works
   100	
   101	- **Genre:** lively illustrated nonsense literature and rhyming picture books. Wave C. ID `tumbletown-workshop`.
   102	- **Emotional target:** improbable, playful, hand-drawn invention.
   103	- **Composition/materials:** crooked towers, looping stairways, accordion lifts, sketchy ink outlines, textured cream paper and candy-striped machinery. Create original geometry rather than tracing a book illustration.
   104	- **Art swatches:** turquoise `#469FA2`, coral `#DF7962`, marigold `#D5AC46`, paper `#F6EEDB`.
   105	- **Cast order:** folded-paper crane maker; felt bell-shaped tinkerer; long-legged teapot creature; concertina-bodied clerk; spool-tailed courier; umbrella-eared inspector. Run badges are separate UI; no existing picture-book character designs or copied verse.
   106	- **Stations:** notion desk / contraption yard / cubby tower / measuring table / mayor's window / spring-seat bench.
   107	- **Props:** impossible ruler, paper parcel, bell tool, winding key, umbrella tray, bent desk lamp.
   108	- **Submission signature:** `capsule`, a striped delivery pod with original proportions.
   109	- **Candidate description:** “Impossible little inventions in a town that never learned to draw a straight line.”
   110	
   111	## 8. Starport Shipyard
   112	
   113	- **Genre:** space-adventure engineering crews in a working shipyard. Wave D. ID `orbital-shipyard`.
   114	- **Emotional target:** a capable crew building something ambitious in space.
   115	- **Composition/materials:** modular orbital dock, luminous planet beyond windows, ceramic hull panels, copper service rails and holographic drafting surfaces.
   116	- **Art swatches:** navy `#1A304A`, ice `#A8D4DE`, copper `#BB8265`, cloud `#E3EAF0`.
   117	- **Cast order:** spider-legged repair unit; translucent alien surveyor; modular tool robot; suited station engineer; floating archive unit; multi-armed inspector. No recognizable robot silhouettes, uniforms, emblems, ships, weapons or audio from existing franchises.
   118	- **Stations:** navigation desk / assembly bay / cargo archive / systems inspection / command desk / docking cradle.
   119	- **Props:** modular panel, diagnostic wand, cargo token, drafting projector, tool case, relay puck.
   120	- **Submission signature:** `spark`, a short projector highlight over a delivered panel.
   121	- **Candidate description:** “An orbital crew coordinates your work among the stars.”
   122	
   123	## 9. Critter Expedition Camp
   124	
   125	- **Genre:** creature-companion teams and natural-history expeditions. Wave D. ID `wildlight-camp`.
   126	- **Emotional target:** discovery, variety, affection and collaboration.
   127	- **Composition/materials:** forest field station, canvas awnings, specimen shelves, glowing terrariums and illustrated journals.
   128	- **Art swatches:** fern `#4E795F`, sky `#90BCCA`, clay `#BB816A`, parchment `#F1E6CF`.
   129	- **Cast order:** lantern-backed beetle creature; leaf-frilled quadruped; pebble fox-like original species; reed-winged bird; coral-antlered crawler; cloud-bodied amphibian. Artist must develop distinct anatomy; no redesigns of existing collectible creatures, capture devices, type symbols or copied interface.
   130	- **Stations:** field journal / sample workshop / specimen archive / observation bench / expedition desk / camp rest.
   131	- **Props:** specimen tray, notebook, canvas pouch, survey flag, lantern, terrarium.
   132	- **Submission signature:** `lantern`, a brief glow from an original specimen container.
   133	- **Candidate description:** “A curious creature crew gathers findings at a lively research camp.”
   134	
   135	## 10. Blockworks Foundry
   136	
   137	- **Genre:** modular building games and voxel geometry. Wave D. ID `voxel-foundry`.
   138	- **Emotional target:** tangible assembly, creativity and readable structure.
   139	- **Composition/materials:** beveled geometric models, terrazzo platforms, ceramic modules and gantry cranes. Use original materials/palette; no copied block textures, creatures, items or branding from existing games.
   140	- **Art swatches:** terracotta `#C27C60`, teal `#4B9790`, sand `#DDCCAA`, charcoal `#34404C`.
   141	- **Cast order:** wedge-bodied maker; cylindrical survey unit; hexagonal mechanic; faceted courier; arch-bodied archivist; small tracked inspector. Shared scene uses geometry as an art language, not a reproduction of game characters.
   142	- **Stations:** pattern desk / assembly platform / component store / fit-check bay / foreman station / staging shelf.
   143	- **Props:** modular arch, crane hook, design tile, measure block, component tray, toolbox.
   144	- **Submission signature:** `parcel`, a component tray slides into place; no simulated percentage or fabricated construction progress.
   145	- **Candidate description:** “A geometric builder's yard where work takes visible shape.”
   146	
   147	## 11. The Cloudspring Baths
   148	
   149	- **Genre:** atmospheric hot-spring bathhouses and quiet, unhurried hospitality. Wave E. ID `cloudspring-bathhouse`.
   150	- **Emotional target:** restorative calm, warmth and deliberate care.
   151	- **Composition/materials:** an original mountainside retreat, ceramic channels, lacquered timber, translucent screens and slow steam. Quiet mode is especially suited, but motion default still follows global preference.
   152	- **Art swatches:** jade `#5F8E80`, russet `#A7614D`, lantern `#E2B976`, mist `#EEE9DE`.
   153	- **Cast order:** porcelain attendants of six distinct silhouettes: crane-like, kettle-shaped, broad basin, tall reed, folded towel, round lantern. No existing film creatures, copied uniforms or film layouts.
   154	- **Stations:** reception ledger / restoration bench / linen archive / quality table / caretaker desk / tea alcove.
   155	- **Props:** ledger, folded cloth, ceramic tray, steam vessel, lantern, wooden token.
   156	- **Submission signature:** `ripple`, contained in a small receiving basin; does not obscure text.
   157	- **Candidate description:** “A lantern-lit retreat brings quiet care to the working day.”
   158	
   159	## 12. Thimble Town
   160	
   161	- **Genre:** miniature people and found-object craftsmanship. Wave E. ID `button-and-spool`.
   162	- **Emotional target:** ingenious small-scale craft and tactile charm.
   163	- **Composition/materials:** spool elevators, matchbox drawers, thimble lamps, fabric awnings and paperclip rails. Original miniature inhabitants, not adaptations of named literary characters or screen designs.
   164	- **Art swatches:** denim `#627E94`, linen `#E7DDC7`, thread red `#B86D64`, walnut `#695646`.
   165	- **Cast order:** stitcher; measuring specialist; paper engineer; thread courier; drawer archivist; loupe inspector. Clothes and tools use original combinations and readable silhouettes.
   166	- **Stations:** pattern desk / assembly mat / matchbox archive / measurement table / workshop lead / pincushion rest.
   167	- **Props:** button token, spool, folded pattern, paperclip tool, measuring tape, thimble.
   168	- **Submission signature:** `parcel`, an original paper wrapper tied with thread.
   169	- **Candidate description:** “Tiny craftspeople make extraordinary use of ordinary things.”
   170	
   171	## 13. Clockwork Stargazers
   172	
   173	- **Genre:** original celestial/clockwork direction from exploration; no single franchise target. Wave E. ID `clockwork-observatory`.
   174	- **Emotional target:** precision, discovery and contemplative elegance.
   175	- **Composition/materials:** midnight domes, brass orreries, ivory star charts, frosted lenses and polished instrument tables.
   176	- **Art swatches:** indigo `#283553`, brass `#BA9A5A`, ivory `#EEE5D2`, star blue `#91BBD4`.
   177	- **Cast order:** telescope automaton; compass-bodied cartographer; pendulum clerk; lens courier; gear-bodied engineer; sextant inspector. Celestial marks are decorative, not generated engineering measurements.
   178	- **Stations:** chart desk / instrument workshop / celestial archive / calibration table / chief observer / winding alcove.
   179	- **Props:** chart, lens, winding key, compass, instrument case, brass token.
   180	- **Submission signature:** `spark`, one original star-chart accent without implying a check passed.
   181	- **Candidate description:** “Clockwork observers turn careful work into new discoveries.”
   182	
   183	## 14. Reef Town
   184	
   185	- **Genre:** original reef-community direction; broad underwater animation. Wave E. ID `coral-commons`.
   186	- **Emotional target:** buoyancy, biodiversity and cooperative energy.
   187	- **Composition/materials:** sea-glass desks, coral terraces, shell archives, shaft lighting and original bioluminescent plants.
