     1	# Handoff posture: implemented overlay themes
     2	
     3	Date: 2026-10-26. Delivery scope: implemented shared Floor engine, fifteen original art packs, standalone local review preview, source patch, user/art guides and retained technical verification.
     4	
     5	Implementation is committed on `feat/overlay-themes` in the isolated worktree. Source/build identity is bound in the performance report. The branch is pushed as draft PR #12 against the buildout branch; no merge or public deployment is performed. Existing old change records' unrelated publication permissions are not reused.
     6	
     7	The fifteen original worlds are complete and usable in explicitly labelled local draft evaluation. Each has six character variants, a scene, props, thumbnail, editable SVG sources and provenance. Normal builds exclude the draft demo and unapproved art; released-mode gallery admission remains pack/hash/title/version bound. Public art records remain empty because no human art/distribution decision has occurred. No exact franchise pack or public “inspired by” wording is claimed legally cleared.
     8	
     9	Observed checks (2026-10-30): 97 web tests, 17 Python tool tests, 26 Chromium/Firefox browser flows including build isolation, dedicated public-output and legacy-fallback checks, web typecheck/build, asset/hash/budget checks and production dependency-license gate pass. All fifteen reference-machine 36-entity performance samples meet the specified frame/switch/load targets. These results do not certify the underlying backend or all devices.
    10	
    11	Remaining release decisions: actual human art/attribution/distribution review; real Safari/iOS, mobile-device and manual screen-reader checks. WebKit could not launch here because required OS libraries are unavailable. The fresh code review's eight findings were reproduced and fixed in one regression-backed pass; no second fresh review is claimed.
    12	
    13	Local review instructions are in [the user guide](../../../docs/overlay-themes/user-guide.md). The delivered preview uses synthetic examples and needs no backend. Feature-level rollback disables both flags and rebuilds; pack-level rollback removes the affected release entry and rebuilds. Existing domain data is never mutated by this feature.
    14	
    15	Worktree/branch are preserved for further work. No protected-surface authorization was needed because no kernel decisions, policies, red-team fixtures, CI workflows or wire contracts were changed.
    16	
    17	[Basis](basis.md), [risk](risk.md), [plan](plan.md), [trace](trace.md), [verification](verification.md).
    18	
    19	Monitoring after any release: watch the originality scan and asset gate on every change, the performance report against its targets on the reference host, browser-result regressions, and any rights-holder contact (response steps in `docs/overlay-themes/originality.md`). Merge needs the human author's DCO sign-off on the final squash commit (review R8); this record does not supply it.
    20	
    21	## Required links
    22	
    23	[Basis](basis.md), [risk](risk.md), [plan](plan.md), [trace](trace.md), [execution](execution.md), [verification](verification.md), [ship](ship.md).
    24	
    25	## Exit criteria
    26	
    27	Fifteen original worlds are verified as observed, every review finding has a disposition, and the remaining human decisions (art and distribution review, DCO sign-off, merge) are named rather than implied.
    28	
    29	## Source-lineage note
    30	
    31	Workflow basis: https://github.com/FlyFission/nuclear-grade-context-engineering/blob/main/docs/00-standards-foundation/source-map.md. Adapted as a local engineering record, not a compliance certification.

