     1	# Authoring and releasing a world
     2	
     3	The [catalog](../superpowers/specs/2026-10-25-overlay-themes-catalog.md) defines fifteen art briefs and their explicit creative lineage. The [engine specification](../superpowers/specs/2026-10-25-overlay-themes-design.md) defines semantic behavior. Existing public artwork uses original programmatically authored geometry, with no imported reference images, audio, franchise characters, fonts or copied dialogue.
     4	
     5	## Editable sources and exports
     6	
     7	`tools/build_theme_art.py` is the reproducible source generator. It reads the intentionally JSON-shaped literal catalog in `apps/web/src/features/floor/themes/catalog.ts`. Do not run a formatter that converts that generated catalog to non-JSON syntax. Generated descriptor files carry full hashes and are data, not executable theme plugins.
     8	
     9	Each world also has directly editable SVG sources in `design/overlay-themes/<id>/`, with a `source.json` identifying its generator/palette. Treat those SVGs as editable art exports: rerunning the generator overwrites them. To preserve hand edits, update the generator or use a separate export procedure that regenerates hashes, manifests, descriptors and thumbnails from the edited source. Never silently mix hand-edited exports with stale integrity records.
    10	
    11	```sh
    12	python3 tools/build_theme_art.py
    13	python3 tools/check_theme_assets.py --root .
    14	```
    15	
    16	Each pack contains one 1000×600 scene, six distinct 128×128 character assets, six props and one 800×480 thumbnail. Assets are passive SVG images, with an anchor compatible with the shared stations and motion. Six variants can represent any number of workers: the stable run badge distinguishes repetitions. Shared actions and signatures provide motion; do not add theme-specific React components, API calls or state interpretations.
    17	
    18	Functional labels are HTML. SVG exports must contain no scripts, event attributes, style blocks/attributes, foreignObject, remote resources, data URIs, DTD/entities or native SVG animation. Only the checker's allowlisted geometry/gradient/clip elements and attributes are accepted. Local gradient/clip references are permitted. The validator also rejects escaping/symlink paths, missing provenance, mismatched dimensions/hashes/bytes and budget violations. It is a bundled-source validator, not an arbitrary-user-upload sanitizer.
    19	
    20	Output names are `<key>.<first12sha256>.svg`; the full SHA-256 and actual byte count are in `assets.json` and the TypeScript descriptor. The selected pack budget is 1 MiB; a thumbnail is at most 100 KiB; the full thumbnail catalog at most 1.5 MiB. Run the web pack-conformance tests as well: they compare descriptor hashes and manifests with actual bytes. Thumbnail URLs live in the small eager catalog; complete packs load lazily.
    21	
    22	## Art review
    23	
    24	Review every world with the same source-state fixture, at actual scene size, with labels/hit targets, in grayscale and Still mode. Check original silhouettes, readable material/lighting, clear stations, restrained signature effects, long labels, empty/loading/offline scenes and overflow. Include independent keyboard, screen-reader, zoom and contrast review. Automated checks and an author's screenshot inspection do not establish all of these judgments.
    25	
    26	Design notes describe genres only and never name a third-party franchise, in internal briefs or in public (`docs/overlay-themes/originality.md`). Changing a title or adding “inspired by” does not clear copied characters. Keep any unlicensed source references out of the distributed pack. Exact characters, actor likenesses, third-party artwork/music or unresolved similarity concerns require specific permission or qualified review appropriate to intended distribution.
    27	
    28	## Human release record
    29	
    30	All authored packs initially remain `development`. After actual human review, a designated release owner can mark an individual descriptor `released`, set `releaseRecordId`, and add a record to `themes/release-manifest.json` containing:
    31	
    32	- Stable review ID, pack ID/version and original title.
    33	- Ordered full asset hashes (scene, thumbnail, six characters, then props).
    34	- `approvedInfluenceText` as an explicit empty string; the release checker refuses any other value.
    35	- Actual reviewer/date, evidence reference, and authorized distribution.
    36	
    37	The gate checks record completeness and hash/title/version binding. It cannot determine whether a reviewer's legal judgment is sound. Do not fill these fields with an agent pretending a human approved the art. A modified art/title/version bundle invalidates its prior record; recapture review for that changed bundle.
    38	
    39	The engine is Apache-2.0. Original authored SVGs carry their own Apache-2.0 notices. If future packs contain licensed third-party material, keep it outside the Apache-distributed bundle unless that exact distribution is permitted. Preserve individual source/license evidence and notices. Credits do not relicense assets.
    40	
    41	## Rollback
    42	
    43	Remove only the affected release record, restore the reviewed previous assets/version if appropriate, and rebuild. Keep Plain Floor available. Draft evaluation is for local review and is always labelled; do not turn it on to bypass a missing public release decision.

